ed. So no.\n\nA3: Use row2 + row6 + no 2? Not allowed because 2 uncovered. So only A1.\n\nA4: Use row2 + row6 + row3? counted.\n\nNow consider using row2 but not row6. Then we need to cover 0,1,2 with singletons. Options: 0 can be row0 or row1. 1 can be row10. 2 can be row3 or row7. So number of combinations: 2 (for 0) * 1 (for 1) * 2 (for 2) = 4 subsets. But need to ensure no overlap: row0/1 don't overlap with others. They are singletons. So 4 subsets.\n\nAlso could use row2 + row6 + row3? counted. row2 + row6 + row7? counted.\n\nAlso could use row2 + row6 + row3 + row7? would double cover 2, not allowed.\n\nAlso could use row2"}}],"created":1790960783,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4185,"total_tokens":4953,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-vf3wSYkk4yhIZX3pUHDdPBeU7axkeLIj","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4185,"prompt_ms":511.999,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12234145758661888,"prompt_per_second":8173.844089539237,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2324.615,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.0307887874837025,"predicted_per_second":329.9471095213616}}